From: xPDFSDK team <noreply@xpdfsdk.local>
Date: 2026-06-07
Subject: [PATCH experiment-10] Add render profiling and selective content skip controls

Background
==========
FPDF_RenderPageBitmap() spends most of its time below the public API entry
point. The synchronous API builds a CPDF_PageRenderContext and then drives
CPDF_ProgressiveRenderer with a null pause adapter, so useful attribution
must be collected at the progressive/object-processing layers rather than
only around fpdfsdk/fpdf_view.cpp.

This patch
==========
Adds diagnostic C exports:

  FPDFEx_SetRenderProfileEnabled(int enabled)
  FPDFEx_ResetRenderProfile()
  FPDFEx_GetLastRenderProfile(FPDFEx_RenderProfile*)
  FPDFEx_SetRenderSkipMask(uint32_t skip_mask)

The profiler accumulates nanosecond totals for the public render boundary,
CPDFSDK render setup, progressive traversal, object-list traversal, per-object
rendering, clip, transparency, text/path/image/shading/form dispatch,
fallback background drawing, and soft-mask loading.

The skip mask can intentionally omit text, paths, images, shading, Form
XObjects, transparency handling, and soft masks from subsequent renders. The
output bitmap is expected to be incomplete when any skip bit is enabled; this
is a diagnostic attribution tool, not a visual-correctness mode.

Safety
======
Default state is disabled and skip mask is zero, so normal rendering is
unchanged unless the embedder explicitly enables profiling or skip bits. Live
accumulation is thread-local for low overhead; the completed last profile is
copied to a process-wide snapshot for JNI callers that read it after a worker
thread render finishes.

